Gaussian mixture model of the holdout inversion
  families 4  siblings per family 3  artifacts per class 400  dimension 20
  family separation 12.0  seeds 5  seed values [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]  sibling layout ordered

Siblings are placed along an ordered axis inside each family, because parameterisations
of a transformation are ordered rather than scattered. The holdout conditions are:
  edge      an end of the sibling axis is removed, retained siblings lie on one side only
  interior  a middle sibling is removed, retained siblings lie on both sides
  family    a whole family is removed, no sibling of it remains

AUROC below 0.5 means the novelty score is reliably backwards.

